& =4p(x+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(2,6),$ so we can substitute $x=2$ and $y=6$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4p(x+4) \\\\ {6}^{2} & =4p(2+4) \\\\ 36 & =24p \\\\ p & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4p(x+4) \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{3}{2})(x+4) \\\\ {y}^{2} & =6(x+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373708 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373709 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373708 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373710 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373708 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373711 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373708 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373712 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373708 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373713 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373708 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373708 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373708 1079 #edb/ref 17592186373711 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373708 1080 #uuid "5942b929-5089-5214-907e-e7493d6e67ef" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373709 1081 "{y}^{2}=3(x+4)" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373709 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373709 1084 #uuid "4679e248-6c42-5b10-a7f5-85a11d3b7d85" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373710 1081 "{y}^{2}=-3(x+4)" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373710 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373710 1084 #uuid "856d50e5-77b1-5abd-9e58-dd5120b3b2d3" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373711 1081 "{y}^{2}=6(x+4)" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373711 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373711 1084 #uuid "7564d90f-3072-5560-97a2-b7637953b396" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373712 1081 "(y+4)^{2}=6x" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373712 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373712 1084 #uuid "a857ee56-5af2-5972-87ed-e38d87eec7d2" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373713 1081 "{y}^{2}=-6(x+4)" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373713 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373713 1084 #uuid "ec7465ca-5d48-5f3f-a89c-d3a97da947e2" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373714 1068 #edb/ref 17592186373715 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373714 1069 "q-119162" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373714 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373714 1071 "The volume of a cylinder increases at a rate inversely proportional to its height. Write down a differential equation describing the rate of change of the height, $h(t),$ in this process. Assume that the radius of the cylinder does not change and that $K>0.$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373714 1072 #uuid "a1f7831a-b17a-51fb-b856-65c1e5eaee38" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373714 1074 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **volume** of a cylinder **increases** at a rate **inversely proportional** to its **height**.* \n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *volume $V$ of a cylinder* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ *increases* at a rate *inversely proportional to the height $h.$* Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{h},\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0.$\n\nWe wish to use this information to find an expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe volume $V$ of a cylinder is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this equation with respect to $t,$ and using the fact that the radius of the cylinder does not change, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\pi {r}^{2}h) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\pi {r}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{k}{h} \\\\ \\pi {r}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{k}{h} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{(\\frac{k}{h})}{\\pi {r}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{k}{\\pi {r}^{2}h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now introduce a new constant:\n\n$$\nK=\\frac{k}{\\pi {r}^{2}}>0\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{K}{h}.\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373715 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373716 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373715 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373717 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373715 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373718 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373715 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373719 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373715 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373720 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373715 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373715 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373715 1079 #edb/ref 17592186373717 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373715 1080 #uuid "b6b289cf-37d4-53ba-b515-6ded603baf24" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373716 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}=K{h}^{2}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373716 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373716 1084 #uuid "95ff1bca-2c6f-5a26-8722-faafc6568b3d" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373717 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{K}{h}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373717 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [1759218