$ to the $y$-axis. The derivative at the point $(3,-5)$ equals $24.$ What differential equation describes this curve?" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373868 1072 #uuid "e6b89f7e-afce-55f3-8c93-dbf9b7119d01" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373868 1074 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*At each point $P$ on a particular curve, the **derivative** ${y}^{′}(x)$ is **proportional** to the **shortest distance from $P$ to the $y$-axis**.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The *shortest distance from $P$ to the $y$-axis* is given by $|x|.$\n\n- Since the *derivative* is *proportional to* the shortest distance from $P$ to the $y$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)=k\\cdot |x|\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant.\n\nSo, our differential equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)=k|x|.\n$$\n\nIn addition, we're told that ${y}^{′}(x)=24$ when at the point $(3,-5).$ We can use this to determine the value of the coefficient $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24=k|3|\\,⟹\\,k=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the differential equation describing the curve is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)=8|x|.\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373869 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373870 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373869 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373871 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373869 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373872 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373869 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373873 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373869 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373874 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373869 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373869 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373869 1079 #edb/ref 17592186373871 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373869 1080 #uuid "81b73e2e-d50c-5e49-8505-3ee73aad8826" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373870 1081 "{y}^{′}(x)=3|x|" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373870 1083 #edb/ref 175921860