ed}| \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(x-1){e}^{2x+2y}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}(u-1){e}^{2v}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}(u-1){e}^{2v}|1|\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(u-1)[{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{e}^{2v}\\,dv]du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(u-1){[\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2v}]}_{-1}^{1}\\,dv \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-{e}^{-2}}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(u-1)\\,dv \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-{e}^{-2}}{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}-u]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-{e}^{-2}}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={e}^{2}-{e}^{-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373937 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373938 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373937 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373939 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373937 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373940 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373937 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373941 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373937 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373942 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373937 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373937 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373937 1079 #edb/ref 17592186373939 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373937 1080 #uuid "83574290-1e94-5b24-a81e-a0a3bedf25ca" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373938 1081 "1-{e}^{-2}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373938 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373938 1084 #uuid "081fd6aa-767f-5e6c-8063-fd90ac7a2f8b" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [175