71 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373971 1071 "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z+x,\\,y+2z,\\,x-4y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2x-4y$ for $-2\\le x\\le 0$ and $-1\\le y\\le 5.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{5}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373971 1072 #uuid "acc5680d-481f-574e-9c37-7723114fd2f1" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373971 1074 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2u-4v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 0,\\,-1\\le v\\le 5}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u-4v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u-4v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,4,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z+x,\\,y+2z,\\,x-4y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=2u-4v} \\\\  & =⟨2u-4v+u,\\,v+2(2u-4v),\\,u-4v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3u-4v,\\,4u-7v,\\,u-4v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3u-4v,\\,4u-7v,\\,u-4v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\,4,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(3u-4v)\\cdot (-2)+(4u-7v)\\cdot 4+(u-4v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-6u+8v+16u-28v+u-4v \\\\  & =11u-24v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z+x,\\,y+2z,\\,x-4y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(11u-24v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{5}(11u-24v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373972 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373973 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373972 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373974 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373972 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373975 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373972 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373976 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373972 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373977 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373972 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373972 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373972 1079 #edb/ref 17592186373974 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373972 1080 #uuid "f789f76e-872e-5abd-b18f-ca246f894f3b" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373973 1081 "7uv-4v" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373973 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373973 1084 #uuid "5477038f-1f6e-56c9-abc2-d2382dd8493b" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373974 1081 "11u-24v" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373974 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17