{′} & =⟨1,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂x},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨0,\\frac{∂h}{∂z},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & \\frac{∂h}{∂x} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{∂h}{∂z} & 1\\end{aligned}|=⟨\\frac{∂h}{∂x},\\,-1,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂z}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, notice that the $j$-component is negative. Therefore, we select the normal vector that points in the *opposite* direction:\n\n$$\n{r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{x}^{′}=-{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′}=⟨-\\frac{∂h}{∂x},\\,1,\\,-\\frac{∂h}{∂z}⟩\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,z))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{∂h}{∂x},\\,1,\\,-\\frac{∂h}{∂z}⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂x}+Q-R\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373987 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373988 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373989 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373990 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373991 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373986 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373986 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373986 1079 #edb/ref 17592186373990 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373986 1080 #uuid "2c9eea5b-e0c0-5c9a-bb50-8a16e942de63" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373987 1081 "P,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂z},\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂x}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373987 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186373987 1084 #uuid "333cd0c0-ea57-5e53-975d-79f76fb18013" 13194139533451 175921