peratorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =3{e}^{({\\rho }^{2})^{3/2}} \\\\  & =3{e}^{{\\rho }^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}3{e}^{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})^{3}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}3{e}^{{\\rho }^{3}}\\cdot {\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{\\rho }^{2}{e}^{{\\rho }^{3}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,dϕ\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }d\\theta \\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}3{\\rho }^{2}{e}^{{\\rho }^{3}}\\,d\\rho  \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ]_{ϕ=0}^{ϕ=\\pi }\\cdot [\\theta ]_{\\theta =0}^{\\theta =2\\pi }\\cdot [{e}^{{\\rho }^{3}}]_{\\rho =0}^{\\rho =1}\\,d\\rho  \\\\  & =-(-1-1)\\cdot (2\\pi -0)\\cdot ({e}^{1}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2\\pi \\cdot (e-1) \\\\  & =4\\pi (e-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374056 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374057 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374058 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374059 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374060 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374055 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374055 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374055 1079 #edb/ref 17592186374057 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374055 1080 #uuid "333c1ef5-6e81-5917-899a-cce4a959a51c" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374056 1081 "2\\pi (2e+3)" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374056 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374056 1084 #uuid "b6e52e46-dee8-5e44-b064-03104f5cde33" 1319413953345