rtesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\n$$\n\nNotice that the region $R$ represents the sphere of radius $1$ centered at $(0,1,0).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=2y$ in spherical polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =2y \\\\ {\\rho }^{2} & =2\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ \\\\ \\rho (\\rho -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $\\rho $ cannot be identical to zero on the entire sphere, we must have $\\rho =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ.$\n\n![](images/cd/cd499dfb1a27171f56e9d253e42fec5884260adef1f8ca5e9e2cecd5a4fb45da.png)\n\n \n\nAs a result, we obtain that in spherical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the spherical polar coordinates into the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =f(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{\\rho }^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{1}{{\\rho }^{2}}\\cdot {\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ[\\rho ]_{\\rho =0}^{\\rho =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}\\,d\\theta \\,dϕ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\cdot (2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ-0)\\,d\\theta \\,dϕ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\\,d\\theta \\,dϕ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }2{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ\\,dϕ\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2ϕ\\,dϕ\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={[ϕ-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2ϕ]}_{ϕ=0}^{ϕ=\\pi }\\cdot [-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ]_{\\theta =0}^{\\theta =\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\pi -0)\\cdot (1+1) \\\\  & =2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374077 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374078 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374079 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374080 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374076 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374081 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374076 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374076 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374076 1079 #edb/ref 17592186374080 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374076 1080 #uuid "49fd606f-d3fe-5e2f-a6df-9b759cab274d" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374077 1081 "\\frac{5\\pi }{4}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374077 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374077 1084 #uuid "f3481de2-b0df-5996-b92a-bb7ee79bd613" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374078 1081 "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374078 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374078 1084 #uuid "b8a2513c-f0bb-