s $4$ centered at $(0,0,-4).$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=-8z$ in spherical polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =-8z \\\\ {\\rho }^{2} & =-8\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ \\\\ \\rho (\\rho +8\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $\\rho $ cannot be identical to zero on the entire sphere, we must have $\\rho =-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ.$\n\n![](images/85/851bf8c7b88641026df202119e7f094632ac477a1a7172baf9ec7c8b986d2ec5.png)\n\n \n\nAs a result, we obtain that in spherical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le -8\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le ϕ\\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the spherical polar coordinates into the function $f(x,y,z)={z}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =f(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =(\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)^{2} \\\\  & ={\\rho }^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}{\\rho }^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ\\cdot {\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ}{\\rho }^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374125 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374126 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374125 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374127 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374125 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374128 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374125 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374129 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374125 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374130 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374125 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374125 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374125 1079 #edb/ref 17592186374129 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374125 1080 #uuid "1e569eff-31a5-5a66-a09e-dfb6296fd30d" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374126 1081 "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ." 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374126 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374126 1084 #uuid "bf6e972f-8346-55f5-a120-e2d13c682466" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374127 1081 "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\rho }^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ." 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374127 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374127 1084 #uuid "5e97def2-5282-5478-8554-d48e268655f9" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374128 1081 "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ}{\\rho }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ." 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374128 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374128 1084 #uuid "52068cb1-c213-56bb-81ea-b3d5249dcab2" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374129 1081 "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ}{\\rho }^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ." 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374129 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374129 1084 #uuid "16f7946e-4c07-503d-b226-21a0416fbb38" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374130 1081 "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ}{\\rho }^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\,d\\rho \\,d\\theta \\,dϕ." 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374130 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374130 1084 #uuid "d190edfe-ddd5-5eb7-b10f-b4a8531a7f32" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374131 1068 #edb/ref 17592186374132 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374131 1069 "q-161929" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374131 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374131 1071 "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=x+{y}^{2},\\,v=y+z,\\,w=2z\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(y+z){e}^{x+{y}^{2}}\\,dV,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x+{y}^{2}\\le 3,\\,0\\le y+z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 4}.\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374131 1072 #uuid "0352be10-03ed-5d12-9e9a-501335a3d9bb" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374131 1074 "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x+{y}^{2},\\,v=y+z,\\,w=2z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & ={(u,v,w)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 3,\\,0\\le v\\le 1,\\,0\\le w\\le 8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2y & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}(y+z){e}^{x+{y}^{2}}\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}v{e}^{u}\\cdot |\\frac{1}{2}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{1}{2}v{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{8}\\frac{1}{2}v{e}^{u}\\,dw\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{u}\\,du\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}v\\,dv\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{8}dw \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[{e}^{u}]_{u=0}^{u=3}\\cdot {[\\frac{{v}^{2}}{2}]}_{v=0}^{v=1}\\cdot [w]_{w=0}^{w=8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{3}-1)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}-0)\\cdot (8-0) \\\\  & =2({e}^{3}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374132 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374133 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374132 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374134 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374132 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374135 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374132 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374136 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374132 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374137 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374132 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374132 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374132 1079 #edb/ref 17592186374137 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374132 1080 #uuid "6c5a98d3-da89-51a1-baff-f599217e67d7" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374133 1081 "\\sqrt{2}({e}^{3}-2)" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374133 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374133 1084 #uuid "ae83ac8f-234c-5acd-bbb5-b25a1cc99939" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374134 1081 "2{e}^{3}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374134 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374134 1084 #uuid "8b34f7d1-a718-5683-99cc-2aea4d235600" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374135 1081 "({e}^{3}-1)" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374135 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374135 1084 #uuid "d20aea26-e03e-599a-8c57-858eaa89a312" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374136 1081 "4({e}^{3}-2)" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374136 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374136 1084 #uuid "eecb9e17-6350-5926-b72c-9db686768a31" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374137 1081 "2({e}^{3}-1)" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374137 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374137 1084 #uuid "c52a153b-0694-5e0b-973b-21e39ee2b46c" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374138 1068 #edb/ref 17592186374139 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374138 1069 "q-161931" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374138 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374138 1071 "Use the change of variables \n\n$$\nu=2x+3y,\\,v=-2x+z,\\,w=\\frac{z}{2}\n$$\n\nto evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{z}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+3y)\\,dV,\n$$\n\n \nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le 2x+3y\\le 2\\pi ,\\,0\\le -2x+z\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 6}.\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374138 1072 #uuid "f98ed60b-0dd5-5ecd-92ff-418213f8aa92" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374138 1074 "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\text{ }dV={∭}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=2x+3y,\\,v=-2x+z,\\,w=\\frac{z}{2}\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y,z) \\\\ v(x,y,z) \\\\ w(x,y,z)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & ={(u,v,w)\\,:\\,\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le u\\le 2\\pi ,\\,0\\le v\\le 1,\\,0\\le w\\le 3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\,2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0-(-6)) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}{z}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+3y)\\,dV & ={∭}_{Δ}4{w}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot |\\frac{1}{3}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}\\frac{4}{3}{w}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{4}{3}{w}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,dw\\,dv\\,du \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,du\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,dv\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{4{w}^{2}}{3}dw \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{sin}⁡u]_{u=\\pi /6}^{u=2\\pi }\\cdot {[v]}_{v=0}^{v=1}\\cdot [\\frac{4{w}^{3}}{9}]_{w=0}^{w=3} \\\\  & =(0-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (1-0)\\cdot (12-0) \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374139 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374140 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374139 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374141 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374139 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374142 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374139 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374143 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374139 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374144 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374139 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374139 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 175921860