end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374558 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374559 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374558 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374558 1077 "field-1" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374558 1079 #edb/ref 17592186374559 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374558 1080 #uuid "f613154c-7ed8-5313-9401-3f23528c5069" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374559 1081 "\\frac{422}{9}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374559 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374559 1084 #uuid "3b1a664c-0362-53b6-9280-4375656408b2" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374560 1068 #edb/ref 17592186374561 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374560 1068 #edb/ref 17592186374563 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374560 1069 "q-274603" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374560 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374560 1071 "Express $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)$ in the form $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x+ϕ)$ with $ϕ\\in (0,{90}^{∘}).$\n\n$2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=$\n {{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘})$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374560 1072 #uuid "865f3443-5472-5690-8426-199e283ca83d" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374560 1074 "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =1 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1) \\\\  & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={2}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =4+4 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =8 \\\\ R & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x+{45}^{∘})\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374561 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374562 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374561 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374561 1077 "field-2" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374561 1079 #edb/ref 17592186374562 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374561 1080 #uuid "e01368e2-3c70-5ad0-9171-599c7b996e0b" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374562 1081 "45" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374562 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374562 1084 #uuid "2dde87e8-104d-53fe-90c9-31d1ab2a483f" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374563 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374564 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [1759218637456