igned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plug in the known values into the above expression. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =12x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =12(4)(-1.5) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}t} & =-72.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the cube's surface area is decreasing at a rate of $72\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{s}.$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374621 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374622 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374621 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374621 1077 "field-1" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374621 1079 #edb/ref 17592186374622 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374621 1080 #uuid "9c3dfd8f-2fcf-5673-ab36-222115c8cf2e" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374622 1081 "72" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374622 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374622 1084 #uuid "44bd0684-6a71-5770-9c5f-022b135ea11e" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374623 1068 #edb/ref 17592186374624 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374623 1069 "q-31588" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374623 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374623 1071 "What is the value of ${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374623 1072 #uuid "46f01b36-965c-5aab-a0e7-c33b421d2a82" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374623 1074 "Let $u={log}_{3}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text