\na=\\sqrt{45},\\,b=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{2}}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374645 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374646 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374645 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374645 1077 "field-1" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374645 1079 #edb/ref 17592186374646 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374645 1080 #uuid "60c9fc2b-cd5a-5361-aa95-ea331990e98d" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374646 1081 "\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}x" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374646 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374646 1084 #uuid "4a81613a-4788-5ef8-b909-c787132d3b12" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374647 1068 #edb/ref 17592186374648 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374647 1069 "q-327668" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374647 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374647 1071 "Given that the expression $6\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with $R>0,$ what is the value of $R?$\n\n$R=$ \n{{field-1}}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374647 1072 #uuid "15e1f11e-507f-5457-933a-1a4faf4ce949" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374647 1074 "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n6\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n6\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=6 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={6}^{2}+{8}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =36+64 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =100 \\\\ R & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374648 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374649 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374648 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374648 1077 "field-1" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374648 1079 #edb/ref 17592186374649 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374648 1080 #uuid "6240d107-7763-56f5-baf7-85a7150d30c8" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374649 1081 "10" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374649 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374649 1084 #uuid "c930a0fb-64d6-52ec-98c7-94e497860dfa" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374650 1068 #edb/ref 17592186374651 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374650 1069 "q-327719" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374650 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374650 1071 "Given that the expression $5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$\n\n$ϕ=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374650 1072 #uuid "23fd15f7-5380-5a65-a0ea-786e9979f729" 13