,\\text{gal/min},$ *reactant* leaves at a rate of\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′} & =(4\\,\\frac{\\text{gal}}{\\text{min}})\\cdot (\\frac{Q}{2(95+t)}\\,\\frac{\\text{lb}}{\\text{gal}}) \\\\  & =(4\\,\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{gal}}}{\\text{min}})\\cdot (\\frac{Q}{2(95+t)}\\,\\frac{\\text{lb}}{\\cancel{\\text{gal}}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2Q}{95+t}\\,\\frac{\\text{lb}}{\\text{min}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Calculate the overall rate of change.\n\nThe rate of change equals the rate of entry minus the rate of exit. Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dQ}{dt} & ={Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′}-{Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′} \\\\  & =0-\\frac{2Q}{95+t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dQ}{dt}=-\\frac{2}{95+t}\\,Q.\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Integrate the equation\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{Q}\\cdot \\frac{dQ}{dt} & =-\\frac{4}{190+2t} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{Q}\\cdot \\frac{dQ}{dt}dt & =\\int (-\\frac{4}{190+2t})\\,dt \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{Q}\\cdot \\,dQ & =-2\\int \\frac{1}{95+t}\\,dt \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|Q| & =-2(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|95+t|)+C \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|Q| & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|95+t|+C \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|Q| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(95+t)^{-2}|+C \\\\ |Q| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(95+t)^{-2}|+C} \\\\ Q(t) & =\\frac{A}{(95+t)^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $A=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is a constant of integration.\n\nWe're told that the reactor initially contains $32\\,\\text{lb}$ of reactant. So, we can apply the initial condition $Q(0)=32,$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(0) & =32 \\\\ \\frac{A}{(95+0)^{2}} & =32 \\\\ A & =32(95)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following expression for $Q(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(t) & =\\frac{32(190)^{2}}{(95+t)^{2}} \\\\  & =32{(\\frac{95}{95+t})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let ${t}_{o}$ be the time when the reactor begins to overflow. The reactor has a capacity of $310\\,\\text{gal},$ so we can use the condition $V({t}_{o})=310$ to solve for ${t}_{o}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V({t}_{o}) & =310 \\\\ 190+2{t}_{o} & =310 \\\\ 2{t}_{o} & =120 \\\\ {t}_{o} & =60\\,\\text{min}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the amount of reactant in the reactor at the moment it begins to overflow is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(60) & =32{(\\frac{95}{95+60})}^{2} \\\\  & =32{(\\frac{95}{155})}^{2} \\\\  & ≈12.02\\,\\text{lb},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374868 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374869 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374868 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374870 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374868 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374871 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374868 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374872 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374868 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374873 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374868 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374868 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374868 1079 #edb/ref 17592186374873 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374868 1080 #uuid "617c7a09-689e-563c-b4f9-daf6d3871ab7" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374869 1081 "11.60\\,\\text{lb}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374869 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374869 1084 #uuid "7cb4e1cb-a4d9-5a79-8bad-83176cb4a640" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374870 1081 "11.85\\,\\text{lb}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374870 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374870 1084 #uuid "97b47761-bf18-5c2c-807b-5fbd6eecd397" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374871 1081 "12.46\\,\\text{lb}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374871 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374871 1084 #uuid "f9316b8e-3e20-5a4c-8d57-cf7e0