1 "Determine the differential equation satisfied by the orthogonal trajectories of the family of curves ${y}^{2}=-\\frac{3C}{{x}^{2}},$ where $C\\ne 0$ is a parameter, in terms of $x$ and $y$ only." 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374902 1072 #uuid "8d4d5768-937a-5096-afaf-5a1645a9f0c8" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374902 1074 "Orthogonal trajectories are families of curves that intersect another given family of curves at right angles. In other words, the tangent lines of curves from each family are perpendicular at every intersection point.\n\nLet's determine the slope of the family of curves given by ${y}^{2}=-\\frac{3C}{{x}^{2}}.$ First, we implicitly differentiate with respect to $x$ and solve for the derivative of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{d}{dx}\\,(-\\frac{3C}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\ 2y{y}^{′} & =\\frac{6C}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {y}^{′} & =\\frac{3C}{{x}^{3}y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we must eliminate $C.$ From the original family of curves equation, we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-\\frac{3C}{{x}^{2}}\\,⟹\\,C=-\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{3}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our slope equation, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{3(-\\frac{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}{3})}{{x}^{3}y}=-\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nFor a curve to intersect this family orthogonally, its slope ${y}_{⊥}^{′}$ must be the negative reciprocal of the slope ${y}^{′}$ above. Hence,\n\n$$\n{y}_{⊥}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{{y}^{′}}=-\\frac{1}{(-\\frac{y}{x})}=\\frac{x}{y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the orthogonal trajectories must satisfy\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{x}{y}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: For the original family, since $C\\ne 0,$ we have $y\\ne 0$ whenever $x\\ne 0,$ hence, the slopes are well-defined. Otherwise, when $x=0,$ the curve is not defined." 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374903 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374904 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374903 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374905 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374903 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374906 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374903 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374907 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374903 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374908 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374903 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374903 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374903 1079 #edb/ref 17592186374905 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374903 1080 #uuid "2e5a7bf9-7ed7-5f8d-ae5a-28a81c6b563d" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374904 1081 "\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{x}{y}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374904 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374904 1084 #uuid "0ec044b6-90fe-559a-a74c-8c1d516f1d3d" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374905 1081 "\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{x}{y}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374905 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374905 1084 #uuid "c7063a98-b14b-553b-9bfb-cf179c08a333" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374906 1081 "\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{y}{x}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374906 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374906 1084 #uuid "1de77dd8-d543-5789-9a42-79d550c52e7f" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374907 1081 "\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374907 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374907 1084 #uuid "90d12a8a-d619-544c-845e-eba3e402f696" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374908 1081 "\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y}{x}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374908 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374908 1084 #uuid "bf969a54-d43a-57cd-ae16-f37e51952fc5" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374909 1068 #edb/ref 17592186374910 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374909 1069 "q-337567" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374909 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374909 1071 "Find the orthogonal trajectories of the family of curves ${e}^{x}=y-C,$ where $C$ and $K$ are parameters." 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374909 1072 #uuid "52f3f0d4-9988-5b9b-b9ad-72185238017c" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374909 1074 "Orthogonal trajectories are families of curves that intersect another given family of curves at right angles. In other words, the tangent lines of curves from each family are perpendicular at every intersection point.\n\nLet's determine the slope of the family of curves given by ${e}^{x}=y-C.$ First, we implicitly differentiate with respect to $x$ and solve for the derivative of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\,({e}^{x}) & =\\frac{d}{dx}(y-C) \\\\ {e}^{x} & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {y}^{′} & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the parameter $C$ has already been eliminated.\n\nFor a curve to intersect this family orthogonally, its slope ${y}_{⊥}^{′}$ must be the negative reciprocal of the slope ${y}^{′}$ above. Hence,\n\n$$\n{y}_{⊥}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{{y}^{′}}=-\\frac{1}{({e}^{x})}=-{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nHence, the orthogonal trajectories must satisfy\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=-{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nTo find the general solution, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =-{e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{dy}{dx}\\,dx & =\\int (-{e}^{-x})\\,dx \\\\ \\int 1\\,dy & =\\int (-{e}^{-x})\\,dx \\\\ y & ={e}^{-x}+K\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K$ is a constant of integration.\n\nTherefore, the orthogonal trajectories of the family of curves ${e}^{x}=y-C,$ where $C$ is a parameter, are given by\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-x}+K,\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is a parameter. Some curves from each family for specific parameter values are given in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/b8/b8ce7390522ca1ba25635d029bdcea9dcec913d4b97a93ff18b5dd5dd6d02834.png)\n\n**Note**: For the slopes ${y}^{′}$ and ${y}_{⊥}^{′},$ we divide by ${y}^{′}$ and ${e}^{x},$ respectively. So, the orthogonal trajectories are only defined on the region where ${e}^{x}\\ne 0.$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374910 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374911 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374910 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374912 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374910 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374913 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374910 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374914 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374910 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374915 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374910 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374910 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374910 1079 #edb/ref 17592186374915 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374910 1080 #uuid "e522c6cb-f9d6-5987-ad61-528a8ff7da2c" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374911 1081 "{x}^{2}y=K" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374911 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374911 1084 #uuid "9b973018-021e-5257-9f64-7b1dca8f2936" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374912 1081 "x=Ky" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374912 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374912 1084 #uuid "3f074d25-df8c-5f17-9004-9d4819ded463" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374913 1081 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=K" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374913 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374913 1084 #uuid "fbdd289a-1e29-5208-9614-ec518ec0edcb" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374914 1081 "y=Kx" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374914 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374914 1084 #uuid "438897e7-ffe3-5941-b12d-caf4ad481d23" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374915 1081 "y={e}^{-x}+K" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374915 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374915 1084 #uuid "7eaf5a30-ace3-555d-865a-9cf9c37b4163" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374916 1068 #edb/ref 17592186374917 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374916 1069 "q-337569" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374916 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374916 1071 "Find the orthogonal trajectories of the family of curves ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=C,$ where $C$ and $K$ are parameters." 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374916 1072 #uuid "20e84823-52da-5d8d-9751-7e5bcade7fd3" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374916 1074 "Orthogonal trajectories are families of curves that intersect another given family of curves at right angles. In other words, the tangent lines of curves from each family are perpendicular at every intersection point.\n\nLet's determine the slope of the family of curves given by ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=C.$ First, we implicitly differentiate with respect to $x$ and solve for the derivative of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}\\,({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{d}{dx}(C) \\\\ 2x+2y{y}^{′} & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′} & =-\\frac{x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the parameter $C$ has already been eliminated.\n\nFor a curve to intersect this family orthogonally, its slope ${y}_{⊥}^{′}$ must be the negative reciprocal of the slope ${y}^{′}$ above. Hence,\n\n$$\n{y}_{⊥}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{{y}^{′}}=-\\frac{1}{(-\\frac{x}{y})}=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nHence, the orthogonal trajectories must satisfy\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nTo find the general solution, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{dy}{dx}\\,dx & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,dx \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,dy & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,dx \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+{K}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x| & ={K}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| & ={K}_{1} \\\\ \\frac{y}{x} & =K \\\\ y & =Kx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K=\\pm {e}^{{K}_{1}}$ is a constant of integration.\n\nTherefore, the orthogonal trajectories of the family of curves ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=C,$ where $C$ is a parameter, are given by\n\n$$\ny=Kx,\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is a parameter. Some curves from each family for specific parameter values are given in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/ca/ca980af3c5db940a9ab95567dfaa1a69ea8afb9f4f42f772bb446df67df129b8.png)\n\n**Note**: For the slopes ${y}^{′}$ and ${y}_{⊥}^{′},$ we divide by $y$ and $x,$ respectively. So, the orthogonal trajectories are only defined on the region $x,y\\ne 0.$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374917 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374918 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374917 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374919 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374917 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374920 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374917 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374921 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374917 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374922 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374917 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374917 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374917 1079 #edb/ref 17592186374921 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374917 1080 #uuid "ba512409-31cf-5e9d-99b6-4d1f84e3bf75" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374918 1081 "{x}^{2}y=K" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374918 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374918 1084 #uuid "833addb7-0164-5f7c-bb34-29651996fbc7" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374919 1081 "x=Ky" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374919 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374919 1084 #uuid "bb7ee723-e1fc-538d-a9fe-fe42e7426afa" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374920 1081 "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=K" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374920 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374920 1084 #uuid "75811765-47db-5662-b560-125a09e37856" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374921 1081 "y=Kx" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374921 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374921 1084 #uuid "e791fc1a-5891-5df4-bee0-fa25c7da72b9" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374922 1081 "xy=K" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374922 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374922 1084 #uuid "1faceebb-b201-5935-b797-b0dcbc04a0d7" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374923 1068 #edb/ref 17592186374924 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374923 1069 "q-337577" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374923 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374923 1071 "Find the orthogonal trajectories of the family of curves $y={x}^{2}+C,$ where $C$ and $K$ are parameters." 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374923 1072 #uuid "95e7abe8-3e12-5829-b71d-e930b03de0fe" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374923 1074 "Orthogonal trajectories are families of curves that intersect another given family of curves at right angles. In other words, the tangent lines of curves from each family are perpendicular at every intersection point.\n\nLet's determine the slope of the family of curves given by $y={x}^{2}+C.$ First, we implicitly differentiate with respect to $x$ and solve for the derivative of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}(y) & =\\frac{d}{dx}\\,({x}^{2}+C) \\\\ {y}^{′} & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the parameter $C$ has already been eliminated.\n\nFor a curve to intersect this family orthogonally, its slope ${y}_{⊥}^{′}$ must be the negative reciprocal of the slope ${y}^{′}$ above. Hence,\n\n$$\n{y}_{⊥}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{{y}^{′}}=-\\frac{1}{(2x)}=-\\frac{1}{2x}.\n$$\n\nHence, the orthogonal trajectories must satisfy\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{1}{2x}.\n$$\n\nTo find the general solution, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =-\\frac{1}{2x} \\\\ \\int \\frac{dy}{dx}\\,dx & =\\int (-\\frac{1}{2x})\\,dx \\\\ \\int 1\\,dy & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,dx \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+K\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $K$ is a constant of integration.\n\nTherefore, the orthogonal trajectories of the family of curves $y={x}^{2}+C,$ where $C$ is a parameter, are given by\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+K,\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is a parameter. Some curves from each family for specific parameter values are given in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/37/37019d0c75ba56e28d3e2a592b806941b16005ddb906f4aa126547c0925bd14c.png)\n\n**Note**: For the slopes ${y}^{′}$ and ${y}_{⊥}^{′},$ we divide by $x$ when finding ${y}_{⊥}^{′}.$ So, the orthogonal trajectories are only defined on the region $x\\ne 0.$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374924 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374925 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374924 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374926 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374924 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374927 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374924 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374928 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374924 1075 #edb/ref 17592186374929 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374924 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374924 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374924 1079 #edb/ref 17592186374929 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374924 1080 #uuid "4e59c1a4-b0c0-53ec-bffd-738ded8226df" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186374925 1081 "x=Ky" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true