6375099 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{20k}{t},\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375099 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375099 1084 #uuid "e5da7e3c-77d2-5ca9-b42f-96f1fc1b286f" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375100 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{t}+20,\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375100 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375100 1084 #uuid "bc8b148c-8534-52bd-9ef6-fec8d4beba7a" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375101 1081 "\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{kP}{t}+20,\\,\\,k>0" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375101 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375101 1084 #uuid "a9a7809f-d701-5477-aae0-f68675e1430c" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375102 1068 #edb/ref 17592186375103 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375102 1069 "q-38357" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375102 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375102 1071 "$$\n[T]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{C}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $C$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $B.$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375102 1072 #uuid "171fe4ce-730c-5fbe-99a6-2dbc5de82526" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375102 1074 "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/2e/2e82c232614bec8a98f079ea56d7913ee13e7b457e33e418198278d2e369fc5c.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}.\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{B}.$ Solving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375103 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375104 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375103 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375105 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375103 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375106 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375103 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375107 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375103 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375108 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375103 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375103 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375103 1079 #edb/ref 17592186375104 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375103 1080 #uuid "4ba2eb2d-11d8-5382-b28d-dd3142a80d57" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375104 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375104 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375104 1084 #uuid "885275fa-0273-572d-b4ee-cd12300d505e" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375105 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375105 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375105 1084 #uuid "132ab69d-5679-5d1c-a1bc-aa2c6fcdc223" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375106 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375106 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375106 1084 #uuid "a56f3d7b-6da1-52d8-acb8-91f8eaa8c91d" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375107 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375107 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375107 1084 #uuid "1bfad28a-987c-5e44-ae2b-d9da6d1bae04" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375108 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375108 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375108 1084 #uuid "86726a21-1a03-57e3-a79b-8a0905cbc6ef" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375109 1068 #edb/ref 17592186375110 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375109 1069 "q-38369" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375109 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375109 1071 "Consider the region $D$ in the $xy$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le 2x+y\\le 5,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nBy performing the change of variables $u=2x+y$ and $v=y,$ the integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(2xy+{x}^{2})\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\ncan be written in terms of $u$ and $v$ as" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375109 1072 #uuid "db1fee9d-f261-54f6-9563-ad9a8f609d1f" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375109 1074 "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dx\\,dy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|du\\,dv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=2x+y,\\,v=y\n$$\n\n \n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 5,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\text{ }\\text{ }1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\nIn this case, we first need to solve the transformation equations\n\n$$\nu=2x+y,\\,v=y\n$$\n\n \nfor $x$ and $y$, which gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{u-v}{2},\\,y=v.\n$$\n\n \n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(2xy+{x}^{2})\\,dx\\,dy & ={∬}_{Δ}[2\\cdot \\frac{u-v}{2}\\cdot v+{(\\frac{u-v}{2})}^{2}]|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}(uv-{v}^{2}+\\frac{{u}^{2}-2uv+{v}^{2}}{4})\\frac{1}{2}\\,du\\,dv \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{5}(2uv-3{v}^{2}+{u}^{2})\\,du\\,dv.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375110 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375111 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375110 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375112 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375110 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375113 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375110 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375114 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375110 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375115 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375110 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375110 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375110 1079 #edb/ref 17592186375112 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375110 1080 #uuid "227ed5b3-0cfb-51b9-820b-b40696387d27" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375111 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{5}(2uv-{u}^{2}+{v}^{2})\\,du\\,dv" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375111 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375111 1084 #uuid "6e43e2c3-5048-5e2e-a94a-bcb90d586202" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375112 1081 "\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{5}(2uv-3{v}^{2}+{u}^{2})\\,du\\,dv" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375112 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375112 1084 #uuid "b13b11c1-2465-561f-a96b-19fa507beb2e" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375113 1081 "\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{5}(uv-{v}^{2}+3{u}^{2})\\,du\\,dv" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true]