dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nFirst, let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of vectors from $B$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ relative to the basis $C.$ To do this, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce $M$ using Gaussian elimination until we get the identity matrix on the left. By doing this, we obtain the required change-of-coordinates matrix on the right.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -10 & 13 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 9 & -11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -10 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -21 & 28\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{7}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -10 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (-4)-(-3)\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375123 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375124 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375123 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375125 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375123 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375126 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375123 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375127 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375123 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375128 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375123 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375123 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375123 1079 #edb/ref 17592186375127 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375123 1080 #uuid "7b21a007-3616-5457-8387-93e955f89993" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375124 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 11 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375124 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375124 1084 #uuid "f79f3f12-b655-5b64-a7bf-a517e67f0b79" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375125 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375125 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375125 1084 #uuid "043754e3-c713-58db-b2fc-5167e1133e99" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375126 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -8 \\\\ 6 & -7\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375126 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375126 1084 #uuid "3c7ce013-3b9e-5223-81e3-0d263fff5950" 131941395