86375166 1068 #edb/ref 17592186375167 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375166 1069 "q-4782" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375166 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375166 1071 "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),$ where $t$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=3$ when $t=0,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t>0.$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375166 1072 #uuid "43272060-66c2-5b16-bbf5-4b06c3b21bff" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375166 1074 "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $x(0)=3.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(0))+C \\\\ 3 & =-\\frac{1}{2}+C \\\\ C & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{7}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t).\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375167 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375168 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375167 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375169 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375167 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375170 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375167 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375171 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375167 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375172 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375167 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375167 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375167 1079 #edb/ref 17592186375169 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375167 1080 #uuid "e617e669-d700-55a0-8fcf-ca8ca72bd6a3" 13194139533451 1759218