[17592186375287 1071 "Find the projection of the intersection between the sphere ${x}^{2}+(y+1)^{2}+{z}^{2}=4$ and the plane $x+z=2$ onto the $xy$-plane." 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375287 1072 #uuid "c752f742-ec7e-5448-8e82-63d4405411e4" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375287 1074 "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xy$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $z.$ First, we solve for $z$ in the equation of the plane, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+z & =2\\,⟹\\,z=2-x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $z$ into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(y+1)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y+1)^{2}+(2-x)^{2} & =4 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y+1)^{2}+(4-4x+{x}^{2}) & =4 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-4x+4+(y+1)^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by completing the square for the variable $x$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-4x+4+(y+1)^{2} & =4 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-4x+2+(y+1)^{2} & =2 \\\\ 2({x}^{2}-2x+1)+(y+1)^{2} & =2 \\\\ 2(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & =2 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection of the intersection is the ellipse $(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{2}=1.$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375288 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375289 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375288 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375290 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375288 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375291 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375288 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375292 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375288 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375293 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375288 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375288 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375288 1079 #edb/ref 17592186375291 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375288 1080 #uuid "9359c400-7f2b-5840-be83-0794f0c7588b" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375289 1081 "{x}^{2}+\\fra