uuid "2d8d4731-859f-5217-921a-45bb7148c36f" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375329 1081 "None of the listed" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375329 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375329 1084 #uuid "cd4804dc-232f-5717-b07c-b3e74fbff1bc" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375330 1081 "images/ef/ef9d0a612a093852fd9f60fb20c86b946c178f9e2a9877ef7c16f89f98e324f6.png" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375330 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375330 1084 #uuid "a9fa7755-b5ce-5247-a0a8-910a9073e68d" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375331 1081 "images/67/67b42d8a49263abc8cce98f20b59370047b989ae69d55050e4001897ba3f9d2e.png" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375331 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375331 1084 #uuid "89301be4-f9a9-59a2-ac5e-5d39c6146fc8" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375332 1081 "images/5e/5eb14fb126d8b0df54e5523d705cb5491e161c00b118f07a0bf3407644b7d4a0.png" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375332 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375332 1084 #uuid "0e509b6d-02de-56c1-a9e8-7efb98174520" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375333 1081 "images/32/3228d2d0c2fb3ce74c98b018c0694e9da5fc4a8444a7b67b5fb7fa0eb24eaa6c.png" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375333 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375333 1084 #uuid "79d18367-2462-5b79-ac87-734c517ed764" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375334 1068 #edb/ref 17592186375335 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375334 1069 "q-72322" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375334 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375334 1071 "![](images/88/8861ad010cbd19d897ace4c8da2fdaeca25e9d2319ab95d3b338e6db49aa21ae.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type I region in two-dimensional space?" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375334 1072 #uuid "b8dcd36b-62ff-51dd-911e-391155781896" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375334 1074 "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type I region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $x:$\n\n$$\nx=y+1\\,⟹\\,y=x-1\n$$\n\nThe function $y=\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}$ is already written as a function of $x.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the vertical lines $x=1$ and $x=3.$ So, we have $1\\le x\\le 3.$\n\nWe draw a vertical arrow through the region to determine the lower function $g(x)$ and the upper function $f(x).$ A vertical line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type I region.\n\n![](images/15/15f9c5d526747b80766a8a3250fa2e705d5d7d9561c52e08492b7a18f1483eb6.png)\n\nThe vertical line enters the region through the lower function $y=\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}$ and leaves through the upper function $y=x-1.$ So, we have $\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le x-1.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le x-1}.\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375335 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375336 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375335 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375337 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375335 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375338 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375335 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375339 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375335 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375340 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375335 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375335 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375335 1079 #edb/ref 17592186375337 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375335 1080 #uuid "06791450-79a7-57ff-982c-0a9c0c48c94a" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375336 1081 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le y+1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375336 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375336 1084 #uuid "94d1678f-c40b-5af3-9c01-5e44121bc63a" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375337 1081 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le x-1}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375337 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375337 1084 #uuid "84793cb4-e8f5-5b93-983f-4e8cd175b741" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375338 1081 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}+1}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375338 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375338 1084 #uuid "ef5ce8c7-a9c2-5498-ac15-36a28bbba91d" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375339 1081 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le y+1}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375339 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375339 1084 #uuid "a8532342-6134-55eb-82d5-4bcf4a8d4a3a" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375340 1081 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le x+1}" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375340 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375340 1084 #uuid "c8beef18-d508-5038-9945-f9210d0f3975" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375341 1068 #edb/ref 17592186375342 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375341 1069 "q-72427" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375341 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375341 1071 "At which points on the curve ${y}^{2}+2x=2xy+2y-2$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $i?$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375341 1072 #uuid "703e7046-bcfc-54c8-9bb1-c367d4d9ddb7" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375341 1074 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+2x & =2xy+2y-2 \\\\ {y}^{2}+2x-2xy-2y & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)={y}^{2}+2x-2xy-2y$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=-2.$  \n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(x,y)={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y) & ={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}+2x-2xy-2y)i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}+2x-2xy-2y)j \\\\  & =(2y-2x-2)\\,i-(2-2y)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $i$, we must have $t\\cdot i=0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot i & =0 \\\\ ((2y-2x-2)\\,i-(2-2y)\\,j)\\cdot i & =0 \\\\ 2y-2x-2 & =0 \\\\ 2(y-x-1) & =0 \\\\ y & =x+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y=x+1$ into the equation of our curve gives:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+2x-2xy-2y & =-2 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+2x-2x(x+1)-2(x+1)+2 & =0 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}-2x(x+1)-2(x+1)+2(x+1) & =0 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}-2x(x+1)-\\cancel{2(x+1)}+\\cancel{2(x+1)} & =0 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}-2x(x+1) & =0 \\\\ (x+1)(x+1-2x) & =0 \\\\ (x+1)(-x+1) & =0 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally:\n\n- If $x=1$, we get $y=2$ and the corresponding point is $(1,2).$\n\n- If $x=-1$, we get $y=0$ and the corresponding point is $(-1,0).$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375342 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375343 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375342 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375344 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375342 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375345 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375342 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375346 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375342 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375347 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375342 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375342 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375342 1079 #edb/ref 17592186375347 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375342 1080 #uuid "079e80ed-3676-528f-b478-841f2caa3b64" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375343 1081 "$(1,-2)$ and $(0,1)$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375343 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375343 1084 #uuid "27399e42-4acc-553e-ba4e-5998ae4da3e8" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375344 1081 "$(-1,2)$ and $(1,0)$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375344 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375344 1084 #uuid "a57c1eee-a86d-5c18-9d82-3d9e99558aee" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375345 1081 "$(1,1)$ and $(2,0)$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375345 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375345 1084 #uuid "bfb1fb31-2625-5bc1-9263-d7661c3e1d2b" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375346 1081 "$(-1,-2)$ and $(1,0)$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375346 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375346 1084 #uuid "ec3841f3-4849-5ca6-b655-2344b4b09e89" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375347 1081 "$(1,2)$ and $(-1,0)$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375347 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375347 1084 #uuid "30f0e009-0c6d-57a0-b587-090a0c1d88bd" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375348 1068 #edb/ref 17592186375349 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375348 1069 "q-73657" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375348 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375348 1071 "What is the value of ${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{6{log}_{8}⁡(2x)}{x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375348 1072 #uuid "1db700ab-3b05-5d1d-a411-1cbed80c9e6b" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375348 1074 "Let $u={log}_{8}⁡(2x).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\cdot 2=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡8}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡8\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1/3$ | $2/3$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{6{log}_{8}⁡(2x)}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{1}^{2}{log}_{8}⁡(2x)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{1/3}^{2/3}u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡8\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{ln}⁡8{\\int }_{1/3}^{2/3}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{ln}⁡8\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}{|}_{1/3}^{2/3} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡8\\cdot (\\frac{4}{9}-\\frac{1}{9}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡8\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375349 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375350 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375349 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375351 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375349 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375352 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375349 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375353 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375349 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375354 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375349 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375349 1077 "selection" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375349 1079 #edb/ref 17592186375351 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375349 1080 #uuid "0cf307e2-aa61-5c5c-9a35-cb1835a62040" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375350 1081 "9\\operatorname{ln}⁡8" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375350 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375350 1084 #uuid "21c7787a-31a6-57b0-b969-bd5a3135ac96" 13194139533451 17592186045585 true] [17592186375351 1081 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡8" 131